course: dictionary
lesson: 3619
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. The word filthy usually means very dirty. «The boots were filthy with mud after the match.» You know the boots were covered in dirt, so filthy means very dirty here.
explain: Now look at «It was filthy weather, so we stayed inside.» Weather cannot be dirty, so filthy must mean something else: very unpleasant. The words around a word are its context, and they tell you which meaning fits.
explain: Some meanings are informal, which means people use them in relaxed speech. «They are filthy rich» means extremely rich, and «She gave me a filthy look» means an angry look. Try the meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Filthy is an adjective, so it describes a noun, as in «filthy boots».
fact: «Filthy» means very dirty, as in «filthy hands».
fact: «Filthy» can also mean very unpleasant, as in «filthy weather».
fact: In informal speech, «filthy rich» means extremely rich, and «a filthy look» means an angry look.
fact: In a story about long ago, Ned says, «everybody filthy», meaning that people were very dirty.
exercise: «The puppy came in from the garden with filthy paws.» What does filthy mean here? | Very quiet | Very hungry | *Very dirty | Very clean and shiny
exercise: «It was filthy weather, so we stayed indoors.» What does filthy mean in this sentence? | Very sunny | Very quiet | *Very unpleasant, with rain and wind | Very tasty
exercise: Grandma says, «Stop giving me that filthy look!» What is a filthy look? | A look at the stars | A dirty face | A happy smile | *An angry look
test: «They are filthy rich, with three cars and a huge house.» What does filthy rich mean? | Very dirty | Very tired | Very poor | *Extremely rich
test: Which word could replace filthy in «filthy weather» without changing the meaning much? | *Horrible | Clean | Sunny | Tasty
exam: Which sentence uses filthy to mean very dirty? | *«Her filthy trainers were covered in mud.» | «He wrote a filthy poem about the sun.» | «The filthy sky was full of stars.» | «The filthy shop had lovely cakes.»
